  "note": "Open: the bands call dmarc_policy_none wrong, because the published policy is quarantine, and expect dmarc_partial_enforcement. The call keeps partial enforcement as expected and makes dmarc_policy_none acceptable: with pct at 0 the policy is applied to no failing mail, so the record protects the domain exactly as much as p=none does. A specialist who describes it as a monitoring-only record in effect is not wrong. It rests on the DMARC RFC's definition of pct as the share of failing mail the policy applies to."
